        "original_id": "8b0061e6-8e40-5509-b44c-dbf7878eab4b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Albany County, Colonie, Latham, Boght Corners, New York\n- Roads: New York State Route 9R, U.S. Route 9\n\nFacts:\n- New York State Route 9R is a north–south state highway in northeastern Albany County, New York, in the United States.\n- New York State Route 9R leaves U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Latham and rejoins U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Boght Corners, and both hamlets are in the town of Colonie.\n- Boght Corners, also called Boght, is a hamlet in the town of Colonie in northern Albany County, New York.\n- Boght Corners straddles U.S. Route 9.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
